        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui-quick): use truncateUtf16Safe for settings source truncation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOne `.slice(0, 34)` truncation site in the Quick Settings UI may cut UTF-16 surrogate pairs in half when the displayed source text contains multi-byte characters such as emoji.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`ui/src/pages/config/quick.ts` uses raw `.slice(0, 34)` for source text truncation. Replacing with `truncateUtf16Safe` ensures truncated output is always valid Unicode.\n\n## User Impact\n\nTruncated source text in Quick Settings remains valid Unicode at existing size limits. No behavioral changes for ASCII-only content.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Mechanical replacement: `.slice(0, 34)` to `truncateUtf16Safe`\n- `truncateUtf16Safe` is already used in other UI files\n- No runtime behavior change for ASCII or valid Unicode input\n\nGenerated with Claude Code",
